{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793185379,"nonce":"0I2o5GRulhSCaQX3qB5JX9qo7Kk=","title":"Mount installed library and extension sources read-only in remote workspaces","message":"Prepared Linux guests keep Haxelib libraries, Haxe and Rayzor standard libraries, and built-in extensions outside the editable checkout. Browser sessions currently cannot read those paths. The embedded Git manifest can also carry a different platform's native hash, so it must not override the actual installed manifest.\n\nAdd bounded operator-selected read-only mounts to session hello and filesystem RPC. Refuse traversal, symlink escape, shared-document subscriptions and mutations against those mounts. Mount them in the browser workspace router and use the actual installed extensions root. Dependency source tabs must stay read-only.\n\nValidate source navigation, exact byte reads, source isolation and native extension metadata with the prepared Linux toolchain and browser session. Related toolchain issue: 2bbf0cb43ce34d42b4903feaa18af7751b5a29071c6ad79942936e8360c2f9a6. Workspace parent: 52138fcda83502ec87679713955f7cf7c7f7e8654a0ef55ba60357bd0f22a904.","files":null}]}